          %h3#observation_2 Observation
          %p (…)
          %h3#NonObservation Non-Observation
          %p
            Cautioning against the interpretation of type Ia
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supernovae"} supernovae
            as indicative of a small positive cosmological constant (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"}> de Sitter spacetime
            ) as in the current
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
            includes the following (see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhomogeneous+cosmology"} inhomogeneous cosmology
            and at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten%27s+Dark+Fantasy"} Witten's Dark Fantasy
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Subir+Sarkar"}> Subir Sarkar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Is the evidence for dark energy secure?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0710.5307"} arXiv:0710.5307
            %li#NielsenGuffantiSarkar16
              %p
                J. T. Nielsen, A. Guffanti &amp;
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Subir+Sarkar"} Subir Sarkar
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Marginal evidence for cosmic acceleration from Type Ia supernovae
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01354"} arXiv:1506.01354
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://4gravitons.wordpress.com/2016/11/11/a-response-from-nielsen-guffanti-and-sarkar/"} web discussion
            %li
              %p
                Koushik Dutta, Ruchika, Anirban Roy, Anjan A. Sen, M.M. Sheikh-Jabbari,
                %em Negative Cosmological Constant is Consistent with Cosmological Data
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.06623"}> arXiv:1808.06623
                )
            %li
              %p
                Rui-Yun Guo, Jing-Fei Zhang, Xin Zhang,
                %em
                  Can the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0
                  tension be resolved in extensions to ΛCDM cosmology?
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02340"}> arXiv:1809.02340
                )
            %li
              %p
                Yijung Kang, Young-Wook Lee, Young-Lo Kim, Chul Chung, Chang Hee Ree,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Early-type Host Galaxies of Type Ia Supernovae. II. Evidence for Luminosity Evolution in Supernova Cosmology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.04903"} arXiv:1912.04903
              %p exposition:
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://phys.org/news/2020-01-evidence-key-assumption-discovery-dark.amp?__twitter_impression=true"} New evidence shows that the key assumption made in the discovery of dark energy is in error
            %li
              %p
                Eleonora Di Valentino, Alessandro Melchiorri, Joseph Silk,
                %em Cosmic Discordance: Planck and luminosity distance data exclude LCDM
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.04935"}> arXiv:2003.04935
                )
              %p
                (preferring
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phantom+dark+energy"} phantom dark energy
            %li#MRS21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roya+Mohayaee"}> Roya Mohayaee
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mohamed+Rameez"} Mohamed Rameez
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Subir+Sarkar"} Subir Sarkar
                %em Do supernovae indicate an accelerating universe?
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.03119"}> arXiv:2106.03119
                )
            %li#SLCPC25
              %p
                Junhyuk Son, Young-Wook Lee, Chul Chung, Seunghyun Park, Hyejeon Cho,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strong progenitor age bias in supernova cosmology – II. Alignment with DESI BAO and signs of a non-accelerating universe
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/staf1685"} doi:10.1093/mnras/staf1685
          %h3#ReferencedInpAQFT In pAQFT
          %p
            Discussion of the cosmological constant in the rigorous formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+AQFT"} perturbative AQFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"} on curved spacetimes
            includes the following.
          %p
            The freedom of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+expectation+value"} vacuum expectation value
            of any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stress-energy+tensor"} stress-energy tensor
          %ul
            %li#Wald78
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wald"}> Robert Wald
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Trace anomaly of a conformally invariant quantum field in curved spacetime
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.17.1477"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.17.1477
          %p
            Notice that (
            %a{:href => "#Wald78"}> Wald 78
            ) is based on
          %ul
            %li#Wald77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wald"}> Robert Wald
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The back reaction effect in particle creation in curved spacetime
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01609833"} doi:10.1007/BF01609833
          %p
            which claimed
            %em no
            freedom of renormalization, but
            %a{:href => "#Wald78"} Wald 78
            explains that this was due to a mistake inherited from a citation.
          %p Further development of this includes
          %ul
            %li#TichyFlanagan98
              %p
                Wolfgang Tichy, Eanna E. Flanagan,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em How unique is the expected stress-energy tensor of a massive scalar field?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9807015"} arXiv:gr-qc/9807015
            %li#Moretti01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valter+Moretti"}> Valter Moretti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Comments on the Stress-Energy Tensor Operator in Curved Spacetime
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0109048"} arXiv:gr-qc/0109048
          %p A useful review is in
          %ul
            %li#Hack15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Paul+Hack"}> Thomas-Paul Hack
              , section 3.2.1,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cosmological Applications of Algebraic Quantum Field Theory in Curved Spacetimes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01869"} arXiv:1506.01869
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-21894-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-21894-6
          %p
            Realization of renormalization of stress-energy/cosmological constant in concrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRW+models"} FRW models
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#DappiaggiFredenhagenPinamonti08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Dappiaggi"}> Claudio Dappiaggi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicola+Pinamonti"} Nicola Pinamonti
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable cosmological models driven by a free quantum scalar field
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0801.2850"} arXiv:0801.2850
            %li#DappiagiHackMollerPinamonti10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Dappiaggi"}> Claudio Dappiaggi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Paul+Hack"} Thomas-Paul Hack
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicola+Pinamonti"} Nicola Pinamonti
                %em Dark Energy from Quantum Matter
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1007.5009"}> arXiv:1007.5009
                )
          %p
            Discussion specifically for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Hack13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Paul+Hack"}> Thomas-Paul Hack
              ,
              %em The Lambda CDM-model in quantum field theory on curved spacetime and Dark Radiation
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1306.3074"}> arXiv:1306.3074
              )
          %p
            More on subtleties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            of the cosmological constant:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Donoghue"}> John Donoghue
              ,
              %em The cosmological constant and the use of cutoffs
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.00728"}> arXiv:2009.00728
              )
          %h3#ReferencesFromHigherCurvatureCorrections From higher curvature corrections
          %p
            Effective dark energy from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+curvature+corrections"} higher curvature corrections
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Starobinsky+model+of+cosmic+inflation"} Starobinsky model of cosmic inflation
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Michal Artymowski, Zygmunt Lalak,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Inflation and dark energy from
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(R)
                    gravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.7818"} arXiv:1405.7818
            %li
              %p
                Michal Artymowski, Zygmunt Lalak, Marek Lewicki,
                %em
                  Inflation and dark energy from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(R)
                  gravity
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.04864"}> arXiv:1510.04864
                )
          %h3#from_inhomogeneous_cosmology From inhomogeneous cosmology
          %p
            Discussion of the cosmological constant as an artefact of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhomogeneous+cosmology"} inhomogeneous cosmology
            (see there for more) includes the following
          %ul
            %li#Buchert07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Buchert"}> Thomas Buchert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dark Energy from structure: a status report
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://xxx.lanl.gov/abs/0707.2153"} arXiv:0707.2153
            %li#GreenWald10
              %p
                Stephen R. Green,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wald"} Robert Wald
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A new framework for analyzing the effects of small scale inhomogeneities in cosmology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4920"} arXiv:1011.4920
            %li#Buchert11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Buchert"}> Thomas Buchert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Toward physical cosmology: focus on inhomogeneous geometry and its non-perturbative effects
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.2016"} arXiv:1103.2016
            %li#BuchertRasanen11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Buchert"}> Thomas Buchert
                , Syksy Rasanen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Backreaction in late-time cosmology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.5335"} arXiv:1112.5335
            %li#GreenWald13
              %p
                Stephen Green,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wald"} Robert Wald
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Examples of backreaction of small scale inhomogeneities in cosmology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.2318"} arxiv:1304.2318
            %li#Scharf13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%BCnter+Scharf"}> Günter Scharf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inhomogeneous cosmology in the cosmic rest frame without dark stuff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Gauge+Theories+--+A+True+Ghost+Story"} Quantum Gauge Theories – A True Ghost Story
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.2695"} arXiv:1312.2695
            %li#BuchertEtAl15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Buchert"} Thomas Buchert
                et. al,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Is there proof that backreaction of inhomogeneities is irrelevant in cosmology?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.07800"} arXiv:1505.07800
              %p
                exposition in
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://cqgplus.com/2016/01/20/the-universe-is-inhomogeneous-does-it-matter/"} The Universe is inhomogeneous. Does it matter?
                CQG+, 2016
            %li#BelejkoKorzynski16
              %p
                Krzysztof Bolejko, Mikołaj Korzyński,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inhomogeneous cosmology and backreaction: Current status and future prospects
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.08222"} arXiv:1612.08222
            %li#DanielssonVanRiet18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"}> Ulf Danielsson
                , Thomas Van Riet,
                %em What if string theory has no de Sitter vacua?
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.01120"}> arXiv:1804.01120
                )
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhomogeneous+cosmology"} inhomogeneous cosmology
          %h3#CCProblemReferences The “cosmological constant problem”
          %p Discussion of the experimentally observed tiny cosmological constant and the folklore theoretical problem with that includes the following
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Subir Sarkar,
                %em New results in cosmology
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0201140"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0201140
                )
            %li
              %p
                Stefanus Nobbenhuis,
                %em The cosmological constant problem – an inspiration for new physics
                PhD thesis (2006) (
                %a{:href => "http://igitur-archive.library.uu.nl/dissertations/2006-0615-200938/"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://igitur-archive.library.uu.nl/dissertations/2006-0615-200938/c1.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Joan Sola,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmological constant and vacuum energy: old and new ideas
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1306.1527"} arXiv:1306.1527
            %li
              %p
                Ioanna Kourkoulou, Alberto Nicolis, Guanhao Sun,
                %em A technical analog of the cosmological constant problem and a solution thereof
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.11620"}> arXiv:2101.11620
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://t.co/0jV2L9R79q?amp=1"} talk rec
          %h3#ReferencesInStringTheory In string theory
          %p
            Discussion from the point of view of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacuum"} perturbative string theory vacuum
          %h4#ReferencesStringTheoryVanishingCC For fundamentally vanishing cc (“Witten’s Dark Fantasy”)
          %p
            An argument for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            4d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            with fundamentally vanishing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
            decompactified at strong coupling to 4d via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            (recall the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+4d"} super 2-brane in 4d
          %ul
            %li#Witten00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Cosmological Constant From The Viewpoint Of String Theory
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/972507"} DM2000
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0002297"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0002297
                )
              %p (see p. 7)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strong coupling and the cosmological constant
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9506101"} arXiv:hep-th/9506101
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , Section 3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some Comments On String Dynamics
                %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/305869"} Strings95
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9507121"}> arXiv:hep-th/9507121
                )
          %p
            This suggestion was called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten%27s+Dark+Fantasy"} Witten's Dark Fantasy
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HeckmannLawrieLinZoccarato19"} Heckmann-Lawrie-Lin-Zoccarato 19, Section 8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            is claimed:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
                , Section 4.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Evidence for F-Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9602022"} arxiv:hep-th/9602022
            %li#HeckmannLawrieLinZoccarato19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"}> Jonathan Heckman
                , Craig Lawrie, Ling Lin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gianluca+Zoccarato"} Gianluca Zoccarato
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-theory and Dark Energy
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.01959"} arXiv:1811.01959
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201900057"} doi:10.1002/prop.201900057
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"}> Jonathan Heckman
                , Craig Lawrie, Ling Lin, Jeremy Sakstein,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gianluca+Zoccarato"} Gianluca Zoccarato
                %em Pixelated Dark Energy
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.10489"}> arXiv:1901.10489
                )
          %h4#for_fundamentally_nonvanishing_cc For fundamentally non-vanishing cc
          %p
            But a) there might be a large space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacua"} perturbative string theory vacua
            and b) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"} de Sitter vacua
            that seem to correspond to observation tend to exist (only) as metastable vacua:
          %ul
            %li#KachruKalloshLindeTrivedi03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shamit+Kachru"}> Shamit Kachru
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renata+Kallosh"} Renata Kallosh
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Linde"} Andrei Linde
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sandip+Trivedi"} Sandip Trivedi
              = succeed "," do
                %em de Sitter Vacua in String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0301240"} arXiv:hep-th/0301240
          %p
            This observation led to the discussion of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"}> landscape of string theory vacua
            ”.
          %p For review see
          %ul
            %li#Kallosh05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renata+Kallosh"}> Renata Kallosh
              , section 3 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em de Sitter vacua and the landscape of string theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/701033/"} spire
          %p However, consistency problems of these arguments are raised in
          %ul
            %li#DanielssonVanRiet18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"}> Ulf Danielsson
              , Thomas Van Riet,
              %em What if string theory has no de Sitter vacua?
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.01120"}> arXiv:1804.01120
              )
        .revisedby
          %p
